                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 31 at 9:44PM MST until September 1 at 12:00AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northern Coconino county, including the\nfollowing areas, Kaibab Plateau and Marble and Glen Canyons.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MST /1 AM MDT/ tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flash flooding will be possible in creeks, normally dry\nwashes, swimming holes, and over recently burned areas. Raging\nkiller currents will be possible in side canyons and narrow slot\ncanyons. Low-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Showers and thunderstorms are expected to continue this evening,\nwith deep monsoonal moisture in place and already saturated soils\nin some locations.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
                "instruction": "Have a way to receive Flash Flood Warnings and be prepared to take\naction should warnings be issued.\n\nConsider changing your plans if you were going to hike, boat, or\npaddleboard to a slot canyon or normally dry wash. If you do still\ndecide to recreate, check in at a nearby visitor center or ranger\nstation.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
